@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title Config seeding and persistence — one chain for LSPs, MCPs, formatters and plugins

' purpose: why only LSPs have a detect→provide→wire chain, why nothing that chain writes survives an sbx run, and the one shape that fixes both
' PARTLY LANDED — steps 1 and 2 of the legend are implemented; 3-5 are not.
'   step 1 · the accessor ......... packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (_proveo_durable_home)
'   step 2 · install location ..... packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (_proveo_tool_home,
'                                   _proveo_container_platform, _proveo_tool_path)
'   step 2 · the carry ............ packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (_proveo_tool_store,
'                                   proveo_sync_tools) · internal/sbx/run.go (SaveStateArgs)
'   step 3 · the named set ........ internal/proveohome/configset.go (ConfigSet)
'   step 3 · the carry ............ packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (proveo_sync_config,
'                                   _proveo_config_tree, _proveo_volume_mounts)
'   step 3b · home-root files ..... internal/manifest (Home.Files) ·
'                                   internal/proveohome (ConfigFiles) ·
'                                   packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (_proveo_config_file)
'   step 4 · the class table ...... packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (_proveo_config_classes,
'                                   _proveo_class_wire, _proveo_class_probe,
'                                   _proveo_mcp_probe, proveo_wire_config)
'   step 5 · the MCP row .......... packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (configure_cecli_mcp) ·
'                                   defs/cecli/Dockerfile · defs/cecli/build.sh
'   the durable root, host-side ... internal/proveohome (Root, UserHome) · cmd/proveo/clean.go (toolRoots)
'   pinned by ..................... internal/contract/tool_home_test.go · cmd/proveo/clean_tool_roots_test.go
'                                   internal/proveohome/proveohome_test.go
'   the one chain that exists ...... packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (§8 ensure_language_servers)
'   where it is wired .............. packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (proveo_seed)
'   the plugin half ................ packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (proveo_enable_claude_lsp_plugins)
'   the durable home ............... internal/proveohome/proveohome.go · cmd/proveo/clean.go (toolSubdirs)
'   the home that is NOT durable ... internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (Home)
'   the copy that stands in for it . packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh (proveo_sync_state)
'   the Serena attempt ............. git 88cefc47 (removed) · _spec/defs/cecli/cecli-paradigm.puml
'   how it failed silently ......... _spec/tests/42-hello-world-e2e.puml
'   the chain, drawn ............... _spec/packages/lib/language-server-provisioning.puml
'   what a class must not assume ... _spec/_runtimes/toolchain-provisioning.puml
'
' ── FOUR CONFIG CLASSES, ONE OF THEM IMPLEMENTED ──────────────────────────
' A harness opens onto a workspace and needs four kinds of thing configured
' before it is useful. They differ only in the file format at the end:
'
'   class       detect                provide             wire
'   ─────────── ───────────────────── ─────────────────── ─────────────────────
'   LSP         _lsp_walk (ext+marker image layer, else   configure_claude_lsp
'               map, ranked by count) mise / ubi          configure_opencode_lsp
'                                                         configure_cursor_lsp
'   MCP         —                     —                   —
'   formatters  —                     —                   —
'   plugins     — (fixed list)        image seed dir      proveo_enable_claude_
'                                                         lsp_plugins
'
' Only the LSP row is a chain. The plugin row is a fixed list against one
' harness's baked marketplace cache. The MCP and formatter rows are empty, and
' nothing in the tree says whether that is a decision or an omission.
'
' ── THE MCP ROW IS EMPTY BECAUSE THE ONE ATTEMPT WAS DELETED ──────────────
' cecli has no native LSP client, so its code intelligence has to arrive as
' MCP — the same delivery cursor uses (mcp-language-server), and the reason
' _spec/packages/lib/steps.puml still names "cecli: Serena MCP toolkit" in the
' MCP-capable branch of the WIRE step. That branch describes code that is gone.
'
' What was there (git 88cefc47 removed it):
'   defs/cecli/Dockerfile      a second venv, /opt/serena, `pip install
'                              serena-agent`, launcher symlinked onto PATH
'   defs/cecli/entrypoint.sh   seed_cecli_serena_mcp — `command -v serena`
'                              gate, then APPEND an mcp-servers block to
'                              ~/.cecli.conf.yml unless one is already declared
'
' The shape was right and the outcome was not: the harness "shipped for weeks
' with its Serena MCP server dead on every boot — a package version skew —
' while the side-effect assertion stayed green" (42-hello-world-e2e.puml). The
' `command -v serena` gate proved a launcher existed. Nothing proved it SERVED.
' The whole feature was then deleted rather than probed, because there was no
' shared chain to hang a probe on: no per-class provide step, no per-class
' health contract, no test that a wired server answers.
'
' ── WHY A HEALTH PROBE IS DECIDABLE HERE AND WAS NOT FOR LSP ──────────────
' language-server-provisioning.puml records a measured refusal: feeding EOF to
' healthy servers returns 124, 2, 1 and 0 depending on the server, so no exit
' code separates healthy from broken and any LSP probe would discard working
' servers. That finding is about LSP stdio, and it does not carry to MCP.
'
' MCP has a handshake with a defined success value: an `initialize` request
' over stdio answers with a result object naming protocolVersion and
' serverInfo. A server that cannot start answers nothing. So the class that
' failed silently is precisely the class that CAN be probed — which is the
' argument for a per-class contract rather than one rule copied across.
'
' ── AND NOTHING ANY OF THEM WRITES SURVIVES AN SBX RUN ────────────────────
' The chain assumes a durable home. _spec/_runtimes/toolchain-provisioning.puml
' states it outright — "PROVEO_HOME is durable and GLOBAL" — and cmd/proveo
' clean.go acts on it, reclaiming `.local/share/mise`, `.local/bin`, `.go` and
' `go` UNDER proveohome.Root(). That is true on docker and false on sbx:
'
'   docker   HOME=/proveo-home, a bind onto ~/.proveo. mise installs into
'            $HOME/.local/share/mise → on the operator's disk. Wired configs
'            land in $HOME/.claude, $HOME/.cursor, $HOME/.config/opencode →
'            same disk. `proveo clean --tools` finds all of it.
'
'   sbx      Home() DELETES HOME and PROVEO_HOME from the run environment, on
'            purpose: sbx runs its own uid-1000 agent and its credential proxy
'            writes .credentials.json into the IMAGE's home, so redirecting
'            HOME orphaned the live credential (ladder rung 3, "Not logged
'            in"). Correct fix, and the cost was never priced: with no
'            redirect, _proveo_agent_home resolves to the image home inside
'            the VM. mise installs there. Wired configs land there. `sbx rm`
'            removes "VM + images + volumes" and takes all of it.
'
' proveo_sync_state is not the answer to this. It copies dirs discovered from
' /proc/mounts — "a block device under $HOME is by definition sandbox-local" —
' which finds sbx's own per-agent session volumes and nothing else. A config
' file the seed writes into a plain directory of the image home is not a block
' device, is never discovered, and is never copied out.
'
' Net: every sbx run re-walks the workspace, re-downloads every language
' server through the GitHub API (60 requests/hour unauthenticated, shared per
' source IP), re-renders every config, and throws the result away at teardown.
' The one exception is the plugin row, which persists because it never left
' the image: the seed dir is baked and the enablement is a merge into files
' that are themselves ephemeral.
'
' ── WHAT CLONE MODE MOVES, AND WHAT IT CANNOT ─────────────────────────────
' sbx runs default to --clone precisely to keep the WORKSPACE off virtiofs: the
' guest's directory entry has been measured vanishing under a running agent
' while the host directory stayed put, after which every Bash spawn exits 1 and
' only a restart heals it. The trigger is a host-side inode replacement of a
' mounted directory (reproduced with `mv` + `mkdir`), which ordinary developer
' tooling does to a checkout constantly.
'
' Clone cannot move the proveo home. SplitNested only lifts binds nested UNDER
' the repository, the home is not one, and it has to stay a host bind or it
' would not persist at all — persisting is its whole job. So the durable root
' IS a virtiofs passthrough, on both clone and non-clone runs.
'
' Which is why step 2 does NOT run the toolchain out of it. Tools install on the
' agent's own disk and are copied across at the edges, the same shape resume
' state already uses — one sequential restore into a fresh VM, a delta save at
' teardown, and no exec crossing virtiofs at all.
'
' One thing on the host still writes that tree: `proveo clean --tools`. Its
' liveness gate could not see an sbx run, because that backend has no egress
' sidecar to count, so it would prune the store a live sandbox is about to save
' into and leave it half written. That gate now counts running sandboxes, and
' treats an unreadable `sbx ls` as undecidable rather than quiet.
'
' ── ONE BUG WORTH KEEPING WRITTEN DOWN ────────────────────────────────────
' `printf '%s' "$SET" | tr ';' '\n'` feeding a `while read` loop drops the LAST
' entry, every time: `read` assigns the variable and returns non-zero on an
' unterminated final line, so the loop condition is already false and the body
' never runs for it. The set is ordered as the manifest declares it, so what
' vanished was whichever subtree came last — cursor's whole `.cursor` tree,
' including the mcp.json step 3 exists to persist. It restored and saved
' `.claude` perfectly while doing nothing at all for the entry beside it, which
' is the shape of failure that reads as "persistence is flaky".
'
' ── THE SPLIT THE FIX HAS TO RESPECT ──────────────────────────────────────
' Two different problems wearing one word. Relocating both is wrong.
'
'   TOOLS    binaries and their registries. Nothing reads them by a fixed
'            path — they are found through PATH — so they can be MOVED to a
'            durable location. MISE_DATA_DIR and MISE_INSTALL_PATH already
'            express exactly that, and PROVEO_STATE_HOME already carries the
'            host path on the backend that needs it.
'
'   CONFIGS  files the agent finds by an absolute path under its own home
'            (~/.claude/settings.json, ~/.cursor/mcp.json,
'            ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json, ~/.cecli.conf.yml). These
'            CANNOT move — moving them is what broke the credential — so they
'            must be COPIED, by name, in both directions, the way resume
'            state already is.

node "The chain, generalised" as CHAIN <<app>> {
  component "**detect** — what this workspace needs\nper class, from the tree" as DET <<app>>
  component "**provide** — image layer first,\nthen mise/venv, else refuse" as PRO <<app>>
  component "**probe** — per-class health\nMCP: ""initialize"" · LSP: none" as PRB <<app>>
  component "**wire** — the harness's own\nconfig format, setdefault merge" as WIRE <<app>>
}

component """proveo_seed <target>""\nthe only step BOTH backends run" as SEED <<app>>

node "docker backend" as DOCK <<host>> {
  database """HOME=/proveo-home""\na bind onto ""~/.proveo""" as DHOME <<db>>
}
node "sbx backend" as SBX <<host>> {
  database "image home in the VM\n""sbx rm"" destroys it" as SHOME <<error>>
  database """PROVEO_STATE_HOME""\nthe host path, already passed" as STATE <<db>>
}

component "**tools** — move them\n""MISE_DATA_DIR"" → durable" as TOOLS <<app>>
component "**configs** — copy them\nnamed set, restore + save" as CFGS <<async>>
cloud "mise registry · ubi → GitHub API\n60 req/h unauthenticated" as NET <<cloud>>

SEED ARROW_MAIN CHAIN : per class, per target
DET ARROW_MAIN PRO
PRO ARROW_CLOUD NET : only when the image layer misses
PRO ARROW_MAIN PRB
PRB ARROW_MAIN WIRE : wire only what ANSWERED
PRB ARROW_ERROR NET : refuse, and say which class

DOCK ARROW_MAIN SEED
SBX ARROW_MAIN SEED
CHAIN ARROW_MAIN DHOME : durable today
CHAIN ARROW_ERROR SHOME : discarded today
TOOLS ARROW_MAIN STATE : relocate
CFGS ARROW_QUEUE STATE : copy, both directions
SHOME ARROW_OPTIONAL CFGS : the agent still reads HERE

note bottom of PRB
  **The step Serena needed and did not have.**
  ""command -v serena"" proved a launcher existed.
  It served nothing for weeks, and the e2e
  side-effect assertion stayed green throughout.
end note

note right of PRB
  **Per-class, not one rule.** LSP stdio has no
  exit code that separates healthy from broken.
  MCP answers ""initialize"" or it does not.
end note

note bottom of SHOME
  **The deletion of HOME was correct.** sbx's
  credential proxy owns the credential file in
  the image home; a redirect orphaned it. The
  cost — an ephemeral root — was never priced.
end note

note bottom of STATE
  **The host path is already in the run.**
  ""Home()"" passes it so teardown can copy resume
  state out. Nothing else reads it yet.
end note

note right of TOOLS
  **Movable: nothing reads them by path.**
  Binaries are found through PATH, so a durable
  data dir costs no redirect the agent can see.
end note

note right of CFGS
  **Not movable.** The agent opens each one by
  an absolute name. Copy by a NAMED set: mount
  discovery finds only sbx's own block-device
  volumes, never a config file.
end note

note top of NET
  **What the discard costs.** Every sbx open
  re-walks, re-downloads, re-renders. ubi asks
  the GitHub API, rate-limited per source IP, so
  a fleet behind one NAT loses intelligence.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in — and what each step must not break**
  ==
  **1. Make the durable root explicit, one accessor.** — LANDED.
  ""_proveo_durable_home"" = ""${PROVEO_STATE_HOME:-$(_proveo_agent_home)}"". On
  docker it resolves to today's answer, so that backend cannot regress; on sbx
  it names the host path for the first time. Nothing moves yet.
  --
  **1b. And make it resolve on every host proveo ships for.** — LANDED.
  ""proveohome\.Root"" read ""HOME"" alone and fell through to ""\."" — which is what a
  PowerShell or cmd proveo got, putting sessions, logs and now toolchains in the
  operator's repository. ""UserHome"" adds ""USERPROFILE"" and ""HOMEDRIVE""+""HOMEPATH"".
  Relocating tools onto a CWD-relative root would have multiplied that bug.
  --
  **2. Give TOOLS a durable home — install locally, sync at the edges.** — LANDED.
  ""MISE_DATA_DIR"", ""MISE_CONFIG_DIR"", ""MISE_STATE_DIR"", ""MISE_CACHE_DIR"",
  ""MISE_INSTALL_PATH"", the ""npm -g --prefix"", ""GOROOT""/""GOPATH"", the jdtls tree and
  the install lock all hang off ""_proveo_tool_home"" — the AGENT's own home, which
  is the VM's own disk on sbx. ""_proveo_tool_store"" is the durable half, and
  ""proveo_sync_tools"" carries the tree between them: restore in ""proveo_seed""
  before provisioning, save in ""SaveStateArgs"" beside the state sync.
  Both namespaced ""toolchains/<os>-<arch>"", the fold pinned against
  ""internal/workspace.normalizeArch"". HOME does not move, so the credential the
  sbx proxy owns is untouched. ""PROVEO_TOOL_SYNC=off"" declines the copy in both
  directions. ""proveo clean --tools"" globs the platform trees, keeps the legacy
  root so nothing already installed strands, and now counts running sandboxes.
  --
  **3. Copy CONFIGS by a NAMED set.** — LANDED, and the set was already written.
  A per-harness list of files would have been a SECOND declaration beside
  ""home\.mounts"", which already names every durable subtree with its ""deny:"".
  ""proveohome\.ConfigSet"" encodes that same declaration host-side and hands it in
  as ""PROVEO_CONFIG_DIRS""; ""proveo_sync_config"" copies it. One declaration, two
  mechanisms: bind mounts on docker, a copy on sbx where a bind nested under
  proveo home cannot be expressed at all.
  --
  **3b. And the two syncs must not both move the same bytes.** Config prunes every
  sbx VOLUME inside a declared subtree, discovered from ""/proc/mounts"" rather than
  named — a volume is state by definition, ""proveo_sync_state"" owns it, and a
  config sync that descended into one would copy transcripts twice and drag
  ""statsig"" and ""shell-snapshots"" into the operator's home, which the state sync
  deliberately skips.
  --
  **3b. Home-ROOT config files needed declaring too.** — LANDED.
  A set derived from ""home\.mounts"" is DIRECTORY-shaped, and two harnesses keep a
  config file beside those subtrees rather than inside one: claudecode's
  ""~/\.claude\.json"" (accepted workspace trust, Chrome onboarding, the operator's
  own MCP servers) and cecli's ""~/\.cecli\.conf\.yml"". docker persists them with
  the whole-home bind and never had to name them; sbx rebuilt both from scratch
  on every open. ""Home\.Files"" declares them, ""Validate"" refuses anything but a
  bare name, and ""PROVEO_CONFIG_FILES"" carries them.
  --
  **4. Generalise the chain into one table and one entry point.** — LANDED.
  ""_proveo_config_classes"" is ""plugin lsp mcp"" — an ORDER, not a preference: the
  plugin row exports ""PROVEO_CLAUDE_LSP_OFFICIAL"" and the lsp row reads it to
  decide which languages to yield. ""_proveo_class_wire <class>:<harness>"" names
  the wiring function, ""_proveo_class_probe <class>"" names the health check, and
  ""proveo_wire_config"" is the single entry point ""proveo_seed"" calls. The
  per-class ""case"" that used to sit in the seed is gone.
  --
  **4b. Formatters are NOT a class.** Resolved by looking rather than deciding:
  the images bake them (""prettier"" in claudecode's) but NO harness has a
  formatter config format, so there is nothing to wire and no wire step to write.
  A formatter is a binary the project's own tooling invokes, which is the
  dependency-tree chain's job. The row is closed, not empty.
  --
  **5. Serena, on that chain, as the MCP row's first entry.** — LANDED.
  ""/opt/serena"" in its own venv (serena-agent and cecli-dev disagree about
  dependency versions), PINNED by ""SERENA_VERSION"" through the same
  ""proveo_agent_version"" resolver the agents use — because an unpinned install is
  precisely what shipped the skew that killed it. ""configure_cecli_mcp"" declares
  it in ""~/\.cecli\.conf\.yml"" only when the handshake ANSWERS, points
  ""--project"" at the scan root rather than ""/app"" (which does not exist on sbx),
  and leaves an existing ""mcp-servers"" block alone — the operator's, or the one
  step 3b just carried back.
  ==
  **Settled on step 2 — install-then-sync, not install-in-place.** Running a
  toolchain straight off the durable root put every ""command -v"", every shim and
  every server exec on virtiofs for the life of the session, and bet that nothing
  on the host would ever replace a directory inode under it. Installing on the
  VM's own disk and copying at the edges pays one sequential restore into a fresh
  VM and a delta save (""_proveo_sync_tree"" is ""cp -an"" plus an overwrite of
  genuinely changed files), and leaves nothing to unlink.
  ==
  **One deviation from step 4 as written.** It asked for a Go twin of the table
  pinned by ""internal/contract"". The table has no Go READER — ""DepLangs"" exists
  because ""internal/workspace"" computes dep copies host-side, and nothing
  host-side wires a config — so a Go copy would exist only to be compared
  against. ""internal/contract"" pins the bash table against the tree instead:
  every named function defined in the lib, every row reachable from the seed, no
  def entrypoint owning one, and the plugin row ahead of the lsp row. That is the
  same shape ""_claude_lsp_plugins"" is already pinned by. If ""--print"" ever reports
  which classes a run will wire, the table is where that reader goes.
  ==
  **Left open on purpose.** Whether the plugin row generalises past claudecode at
  all, given the seed dir is one vendor's marketplace cache; and whether a wired
  config should be RE-wired on every open or only when detection changes, once it
  stops being free.
end legend
@enduml
